<p>President Trump announced new US tariffs on imported brand-name pharmaceuticals, with rates of up to 100% for companies that do not lower prices and move manufacturing to the United States. Generic drugs are exempt, and some companies with US investment commitments will face lower rates or no tariff at all. The administration also revised metals duties, keeping 50% tariffs on unprocessed steel, aluminum, and copper while moving products that contain those metals to a new system that generally charges 10% to 25% and exempts goods with less than 15% metal content by weight. The White House said the measures are meant to close tariff loopholes and bring more pharmaceutical production back to the US, using Section 232 national security authority after investigations. Trump has also cast tariffs as a way to push down drug prices, though the real effect remains unclear. The move comes one year after Trump&#x27;s broader &quot;Liberation Day&quot; tariffs and after the Supreme Court undercut parts of that wider tariff program, pushing the administration toward narrower, sector-based actions. Abroad, Australia quickly said it would not weaken protections that keep common medicines affordable, a sign that the US policy is already shaping debates over pricing and supply chains beyond its borders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OmWM9y8e1t1pH6wgxDRx67trk-nl395QxQmHXRdxuAs9BUUAjG6HZcG6hPnRK8wcD41JSsiBrM7kKEwrihcUlwvN9q6Z-ok1EiVRWptupw-qYYV2io7pNxn0oCrFu7yMXF-xm-dFf8mr9AUO2zeG9N_ZK6ipn1dpFq-YDoiwybp02qc_xhDOOOjP1TW-IBg' alt='President Trump during coverage of the tariff announcement on patented drugs.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Zero-tariff condition: Companies that signed a &quot;most favoured nation&quot; pricing deal and are actively building US facilities for patented pharmaceuticals and their ingredients can get a 0% tariff.</li><li>Metals method: US officials changed the tariff calculation for steel, aluminum, and copper products to use the full value of the metals paid by US buyers rather than what it cost to produce them in a foreign country, saying the revision simplifies compliance.</li><li>Trade deal relief: Countries that already reached trade agreements with the Trump administration will get lower pharmaceutical tariff rates, sharply reducing the number of imported drugs expected to face the maximum duty.</li><li>Loophole rationale: A senior administration official said the tariffs were meant to close loopholes, not respond to affordability concerns, and argued they would not affect shelf prices.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Trump administration: Senior administration officials said the metals rewrite was meant to simplify customs calculations that had confused importers, describing the change as a technical cleanup rather than simply a tariff increase. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/02/trump-new-tariffs-pharmaceuticals-metals-00856242'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Australia: Health minister Mark Butler said the government would not remove price protections on common medicines and would not give in to pressure from drug companies or Washington. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/apr/03/australia-says-it-wont-raise-drug-prices-after-trumps-100-tariff-on-pharmaceuticals-imported-into-us'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Al Jazeera analysis: The outlet said President Trump has framed tariffs as a tool to push down high medicine costs, while also noting that the real effect on consumers remains uncertain. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/2/trump-unveils-100-percent-tariff-on-drugs-to-push-for-pharmaceutical-deals'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/04/02/2026/trump-places-new-tariffs-on-drugs-metals'>Trump places new tariffs on drugs, metals</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/02/trump-new-tariffs-pharmaceuticals-metals-00856242'>Trump imposes tariffs on pharmaceuticals, adjusts duties on steel, other metals</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/4/2/trump-unveils-100-percent-tariff-on-drugs-to-push-for-pharmaceutical-deals'>Trump unveils 100 percent tariff on drugs to push for pharmaceutical deals</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/25ecf952-2fca-4ac0-9f72-69949c929a62'>Trump administration announces new tariffs on pharmaceuticals</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/apr/03/australia-says-it-wont-raise-drug-prices-after-trumps-100-tariff-on-pharmaceuticals-imported-into-us'>Australia says it won’t raise drug prices after Trump’s 100% tariff on pharmaceuticals imported into US</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1saxy8n/trump_signs_order_imposing_100_percent_tariff_on/'>Trump signs order imposing 100 percent tariff on brand name drugs</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-unveils-100-tariff-on-some-patented-drugs-on-liberation-day-anniversary/article70818427.ece'>Trump unveils 100% tariff on some patented drugs on ’Liberation Day’ anniversary</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/wrapup-1-a-year-after-liberation-day-trump-sets-new-drug-tariffs-adjusts-metals-duties'>A year after ‘Liberation Day’, Trump sets new drug tariffs, adjusts metals duties</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>